# Operator allow list this build is reduced to (--include_ops_by_config).
#
# Format: <domain>;<opset>;<Op1>,<Op2>,...
#
# Source models (RAGFlow / EE DeepDoc, converted from PaddlePaddle):
#   OSS:  det.ort, layout.ort (plus the laws/manual/paper domain variants),
#         rec.ort, tsr.ort
#   EE:   det.ee.cpu.ort, layout.ee.cpu.ort, rec.ee.cpu.ort, tsr.ee.cpu.ort
#
# Regenerate this file whenever the models change:
#   onnxruntime/scripts/gen_required_ops.sh --models <dir-with-.ort-files>
# A model that needs an operator missing here fails at runtime with
# "Could not find an implementation for <Op>(<opset>)", so a stale list is a
# production outage, not a build warning.
#
# The com.microsoft entry is REQUIRED, not leftover: PaddlePaddle conversion
# emits fused kernels (FusedConv, FusedMatMul, QuickGelu) and the EE models add
# SkipLayerNormalization. Do not "clean up" this line by adding
# --disable_contrib_ops to the build - that makes every DeepDoc model fail to load.
#
# Operator-set additions for the EE *.ee.cpu.ort models (Fixed optimization
# folds most raw ops away, leaving only these): SimplifiedLayerNormalization
# (ai.onnx;1), SkipLayerNormalization (com.microsoft;1) and ReduceMean
# (ai.onnx;13) are the three genuinely new operators; the rest are the same
# ops the OSS models already use, listed again at the higher opset context the
# EE models import (rec/det = 14, tsr/layout = 17).
ai.onnx;1;Conv,GlobalAveragePool,LayerNormalization,Shape,SimplifiedLayerNormalization,Softmax,Squeeze,Transpose
ai.onnx;4;Concat
ai.onnx;5;Reshape
ai.onnx;6;Clip,Relu,Sigmoid
ai.onnx;7;Add,Div,Mul
ai.onnx;9;BatchNormalization,Cast,MatMul
ai.onnx;10;AveragePool,Slice
ai.onnx;11;AveragePool,Clip,Concat,Conv,ConvTranspose,Resize,TopK
ai.onnx;12;MaxPool
ai.onnx;13;Cast,Clip,Concat,Flatten,GatherElements,MatMul,Mod,ReduceMax,ReduceMean,Resize,Shape,Sigmoid,Slice,Softmax,Split,Squeeze,Tile,Transpose,Unsqueeze
ai.onnx;14;Add,BatchNormalization,Div,Mul,Relu,Reshape,Sub
com.microsoft;1;FusedConv,FusedMatMul,QuickGelu,SkipLayerNormalization
